      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "If $f(x)$ is given by the table shown below, what are its roots?\n\n| $x$ | $-4$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $0$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $16$ | $6$ | $0$ | $1$ | $3$ | $0$ | $16$ | $25$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The roots of the function are the values of $x$ such that $f(x)=0.$ In the given table, we see that $f(-2)=0$ and $f(3)=0.$\n\nTherefore, the roots of the function are $x=-2$ and $x=3.$",
